{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"cdd0b10887a17168a92dd8748cfbaccae832647ee3be443dcbd97a24a2d28105","slug":"algorithms.shor.verification","location":"/algorithms/shor/verification.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Verification: order finding and factoring","description":"Acceptance checks for reversible arithmetic, phase samples, and recovered factors.","authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Open Quantum Algorithms contributors","given":"Open Quantum Algorithms","family":"contributors"},"name":"Open Quantum Algorithms contributors","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"verification.md","url":"/OpenQuantumAlgorithms-site/_public/verification-45a031d443d250e3ee89e5e5ffc8954d.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verification protocol","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"GyN0Yru0ai"}],"key":"apXE9BDOnb"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"These checks are planned acceptance criteria. This page contains no executed Shor result or reproduced formal proof. Method-specific evidence will link to the implemented circuit, pinned environment, and report.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"eVu0lZHsGO"}],"key":"OJ2CrA0MFL"}],"key":"rxZ3B8KkD0"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check arithmetic before factoring","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"key":"cBVeq9p95U"}],"identifier":"check-arithmetic-before-factoring","label":"Check arithmetic before factoring","html_id":"check-arithmetic-before-factoring","implicit":true,"key":"dHTE80M7Tp"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For small registers, compare each modular multiplication with classical integer arithmetic on every valid basis input. Define the circuit’s behavior on basis states outside ","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"rXcAo8EHro"},{"type":"inlineMath","value":"0\\leq x<N","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"html":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\leq x&lt;N</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7804em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5782em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.10903em;\">N</span></span></span></span>","key":"RfYg86VCLY"},{"type":"text","value":" as well: a reversible circuit must have a consistent unitary extension over the entire register. Test the control-off identity, the control-on permutation, register ordering, and restoration of every clean ancilla.","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"DEKBkpVYzB"}],"key":"N5p7a6RSmY"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compare the explicit circuit with its decomposed export up to global phase. A simulator’s classical arithmetic callback or a dense matrix representing the desired permutation is a reference oracle, not evidence that the scalable arithmetic generator has been implemented.","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"W1EWPdBoCX"}],"key":"fs0YTxGsYP"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check the complete attempt","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"qFVM5lfpZC"}],"identifier":"check-the-complete-attempt","label":"Check the complete attempt","html_id":"check-the-complete-attempt","implicit":true,"key":"GZzG0aITI2"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose tiny instances with a classically known multiplicative order. Record the phase samples, the continued-fraction procedure, and every candidate order rejected or accepted. Verify ","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"WZ7UcT6SYK"},{"type":"inlineMath","value":"a^r\\bmod N=1","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"html":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mtext> </mtext><mo lspace=\"0.22em\" rspace=\"0.22em\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a^r\\bmod N=1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><